EXAM_DATA.papers["2008"] = {"id":"2008","year":2008,"label":"2008 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2008/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"The idea that some groups of people may be more intelligent than others is one of those hypotheses that dare not speak its name. But Gregory Cochran is   {{1}}   to say it anyway. He is that   {{2}}   bird, a scientist who works independently   {{3}}   any institution. He helped popularize the idea that some diseases not   {{4}}   thought to have a bacterial cause were actually infections, which aroused much controversy when it was first suggested."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"{{5}}   he, however, might tremble at the   {{6}}   of what he is about to do. Together with another two scientists, he is publishing a paper which not only   {{7}}   that one group of humanity is more intelligent than the others, but explains the process that has brought this about. The group in   {{8}}   is a particular people originated from central Europe. The process is natural selection."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"This group generally does well in IQ test,   {{9}}   12-15 points above the   {{10}}   value of 100, and has contributed   {{11}}   to the intellectual and cultural life of the West, as the   {{12}}   of their elites, including several world-renowned scientists,   {{13}}   . They also suffer more often than most people from a number of nasty genetic diseases, such as breast cancer. These facts,   {{14}}   , have previously been thought unrelated. The former has been   {{15}}   to social effects, such as a strong tradition of   {{16}}   education. The latter was seen as a (an)   {{17}}   of genetic isolation. Dr. Cochran suggests that the intelligence and diseases are intimately   {{18}}   . His argument is that the unusual history of these people has   {{19}}   them to unique evolutionary pressures that have resulted in this   {{20}}   state of affairs."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"selected"},{"key":"B","text":"prepared"},{"key":"C","text":"obliged"},{"key":"D","text":"pleased"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"前句说'此话题没人敢说' 上一句强调这个观点 is one of those hypotheses that dare not speak its name，接着用 But 转折说 Cochran 仍要说，空处描写的是他面对禁忌话题仍敢开口的状态——线索指向'有意愿/有准备地去做'，而不是'被选中'或'被迫'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"selected 意为'被挑选'，原文中 Cochran 是主动开口讲此话题，没有'被某人选中来说'的情节，逻辑不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"prepared 与 to say 搭配为 be prepared to do='愿意/做好准备去做'，紧承 But 的转折语气——别人不敢说，他却愿意/做好准备去说，与 dare not speak its name. But 一脉相承。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"obliged 强调'迫于义务/无奈不得不'，但下文一直把 Cochran 描绘成主动挑战禁区的独立学者，没有任何外力强迫他发声，色彩冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"pleased 指'乐于/高兴'，话题敏感、'might tremble'后文也暗示压力，不会是单纯的'高兴去说'，情绪色彩不匹配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"unique"},{"key":"B","text":"particular"},{"key":"C","text":"special"},{"key":"D","text":"rare"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"同位语解释'罕见'之处 空后的同位语 a scientist who works independently __(3)__ any institution 给出原因——一个独立于任何机构之外的科学家，正是英语里 a rare bird（罕见之人）这一固定说法所形容的对象。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"unique 意为'独一无二'，程度极强，而后文同位语只说他 works independently __(3)__ any institution，不是世上唯一一人，且 a unique bird 不是英语习惯说法。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"particular 多表示'特指的某个'或'挑剔'，并不传达'稀有'，且 a particular bird 不是固定隐喻。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"special 笼统、无'稀有'之意，且与 bird 连用无固定隐喻意义。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"rare 与 bird 组成英语习语 a rare bird，专指'罕见的人/异类'，正好被同位语 a scientist who works independently __(3)__ any institution（独立于任何机构的科学家）所佐证，是同义并行的描述。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"of"},{"key":"B","text":"with"},{"key":"C","text":"in"},{"key":"D","text":"against"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"3.","reason":"independent(ly) of 固定搭配 空所在结构 a scientist who works independently __(3)__ any institution 中，independently 的固定搭配为 independent(ly) of='独立于…之外'，无需跨句寻找。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"of 与 independently 构成 be/work independently of='独立于…之外'，意为他不依附 any institution，与上文 __(2)__ bird 的孤胆形象一致。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"with 表'与…一起'，与 independently'独立地'语义冲突，且没有 independently with 的固定用法。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"in 与 independently 不构成固定搭配，be independent in 之类用法多接抽象品质，不接机构。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"against='反对'，文章说他不附属任何机构，而非与机构对抗，搭配与文意都不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"subsequently"},{"key":"B","text":"presently"},{"key":"C","text":"previously"},{"key":"D","text":"lately"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"原以为非细菌→实际却是感染 原文 some diseases not __(4)__ thought to have a bacterial cause were actually infections 是一种'过去认为…而实际…'的对照——'were actually infections'是被推翻的真相，空处所修饰的 thought 应指'此前/以前曾认为'，时间锚点为'相对于现在/相对于真相被揭示之前'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"subsequently='后来、随后'，但句意要的是'此前曾被认为'，方向相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"presently 多义'目前'或'不久'，无论哪种都不表达'在被推翻之前的旧观点'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"previously='以前'，与后文 were actually infections 形成'previously thought… actually were…'的经典对照，正是 Cochran 所推翻的旧观念。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"lately='最近'，意味着新近的看法，与'被 Cochran 推翻的旧看法'冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Only"},{"key":"B","text":"So"},{"key":"C","text":"Even"},{"key":"D","text":"Hence"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"5.","reason":"前一段塑造他'敢说'，本句却说他'会发抖' 前文 But Gregory Cochran is __(1)__ to say it anyway 强调他敢说；本句 he, however, might tremble at the __(6)__ of what he is about to do 却说他可能也会发抖。前后是'即便如此/再…也…'的让步关系，空里需要表达'连他这样敢说的人都…'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Only he 意为'只有他'，但上文从未把他塑造成'独一无二'，且与 however 表达的让步语气不搭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"So 表'因此/所以'，结果关系，但本句中有 however 表转折，二者逻辑冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Even he='连他这样敢说的人也…'，与后面 however, might tremble 共同构成让步语气：连这样一位敢挑战禁忌的学者都会发怵，凸显他即将做的事之大胆。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Hence='因此'，因果方向，与紧随其后的 however 互斥。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"thought"},{"key":"B","text":"sight"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"risk"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"后接 of 引导的从句内容 空后是 of what he is about to do——'他即将要做的事'，这是一种抽象的预想，而非可看见的实物，所以最契合的是 at the thought of='一想到…就…'这个固定搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"thought 与 at the…of 构成 at the thought of='一想到…'，并与 tremble 高度匹配，意为'一想到自己将做的事，他都会发抖'，与 __(5)__ he, however, might tremble 的让步基调完全一致。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"sight 用于 at the sight of 后接具体可见对象（血、危险场景等），但 what he is about to do 是尚未发生的抽象事件，不可'看见'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"cost 常与 at the cost of='以…为代价'连用，意思偏物质/牺牲，与 tremble 也不直接搭配，文意未提及他付出何种代价。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"risk 多用于 at the risk of='冒…的危险'，强调'冒险去做'，而本句强调的是'仅仅想一想就会发抖'的心理预期，方向有偏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"advises"},{"key":"B","text":"suggests"},{"key":"C","text":"protests"},{"key":"D","text":"objects"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"not only…but explains 并列结构 原文为 a paper which not only __(7)__ that one group of humanity is more intelligent than the others, but explains the process，并列谓语是 explains（解释过程），空里要填的也应是论文'提出/主张'某种观点的中性动词，且能接 that 从句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"advises 后跟 that 从句一般用于'劝告/建议某人做某事'，主语多为人，且强调指令性，不适合论文'提出某种观点'。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"suggests 在学术语体中常意为'表明、提出（观点）'，主语可为论文/证据，与 that 从句搭配自然，并与并列谓语 explains 同为中性陈述，整体表达'论文不仅提出…还解释了…'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"protests 表强烈反对/抗议，但论文的立场是'主张存在群体智力差异'，是支持而非抗议，色彩相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"objects 表'反对'，object to/that 也带否定立场，但论文是在论证一个肯定命题，方向反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"progress"},{"key":"B","text":"fact"},{"key":"C","text":"need"},{"key":"D","text":"question"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"对前句论文主张中那个'人群'的回指 上句 one group of humanity is more intelligent than the others 引出了一个群体，下句 The group in __(8)__ is a particular people originated from central Europe 显然是回指'刚才说到/讨论的那个群体'，最契合 in question='所讨论的、所涉及的'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"progress in progress='进行中'，多用于事件/工程，不修饰人群。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"fact in fact='事实上'是句子状语，不能作 The group 的定语短语。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"need in need='穷困/需要帮助的'，文章并未说该族群需要帮助，逻辑不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"question in question='所讨论的、提及的'，正好回指上句 one group of humanity，是该群体的同义引出。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attaining"},{"key":"B","text":"scoring"},{"key":"C","text":"reaching"},{"key":"D","text":"calculating"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"IQ 测试与高于平均 12-15 分 原文 does well in IQ test, __(9)__ 12-15 points above the __(10)__ value of 100——在 IQ 测试中表现好，'得分'高于平均 12-15 分，宾语是 12-15 points（分数），最自然的搭配是 score points='得分多少分'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"attaining 常与 goal/level/age 搭配，如 attain a high level；用'达到 12-15 分高于平均'不地道，因为 12-15 points above 是分差而非绝对水平。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"scoring 与 points 搭配是英语考试/比赛语境下'得分'的固定说法，scoring 12-15 points above the mean='得分高于平均值 12-15 分'，与 IQ test 的语境完美契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"reaching 可接绝对数值（reaching 115），但这里是'high above the mean'的相对差距，不是直接达到某个具体值。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"calculating 是'计算'，主语应是研究者而非被测群体；该群体是测试中'得分'，不是'计算'分。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"normal"},{"key":"B","text":"common"},{"key":"C","text":"mean"},{"key":"D","text":"total"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"12-15 points above the ___ value of 100 原文 __(9)__ 12-15 points above the __(10)__ value of 100——12-15 分'高于…的 100 分'，IQ 测试中 100 分恰为人群均值（这是 IQ 测验的常识表达），空里要填'平均的'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"normal value 可表'正常值'，但隐含'非异常'判断，IQ=100 在统计上是均值而非'正常区间'，且 normal value 不是 IQ 测试通用术语。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"common value='常见值'，类似于众数概念，但 IQ=100 是均值，不是'最常见的值'。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"mean 在统计学中作形容词意为'平均的'，mean value=均值，正好与 IQ 测验设定均值为 100 这一常识一致；且与前文 __(9)__ 12-15 points above'高于均值 12-15 分'完美搭配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"total value='总值'，IQ 不是累加值，不存在'总分 100'，且'高于总分 12-15 分'更说不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"unconsciously"},{"key":"B","text":"disproportionately"},{"key":"C","text":"indefinitely"},{"key":"D","text":"unaccountably"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"11.","reason":"高 IQ 群体在西方知识与文化中的贡献 原文 has contributed __(11)__ to the intellectual and cultural life of the West, as the __(12)__ of their elites, including several world-renowned scientists, __(13)__——该群体在西方知识文化中的贡献多到与其人口比例不相称（精英职业生涯证明了这一点）；线索指向'与人口比例不相称地'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"unconsciously='无意识地'，多形容个体心理状态，不能形容一个群体对文化的贡献规模。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"disproportionately='不成比例地'，常用于表达'贡献相对于人口比例之大'，与下文 including several world-renowned scientists 这类佐证完美对应——人口少但精英多。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"indefinitely='无限期/无定期地'，是时间维度的副词，与'贡献多少'的程度维度不匹配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"unaccountably='无法解释地'，但文章后半部分恰恰给出了 unique evolutionary pressures 这一解释，与'无法解释'矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"missions"},{"key":"B","text":"fortunes"},{"key":"C","text":"interests"},{"key":"D","text":"careers"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"其精英'怎么了'+包含若干世界知名科学家 原文 as the __(12)__ of their elites, including several world-renowned scientists, __(13)__——后接 including several world-renowned scientists 说明精英们以'世界知名科学家'为代表；最能展现贡献的是他们的'职业生涯/事业成就'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"missions='使命'强调任务方向，但例证用的是'世界知名科学家'，他们的成就主要体现为事业而非'使命'本身。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"fortunes='财富'或'命运'，文章谈的是'对智识与文化的贡献'，而非财富积累，焦点偏离。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"interests='兴趣/利益'是个体属性，难以与'世界知名科学家'这一身份成就直接对接。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"careers 与 elites 搭配指'精英的职业生涯/事业'，正好由 including several world-renowned scientists 举例佐证；用精英的事业成就来印证该群体对西方智识文化贡献巨大，逻辑直接。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"affirm"},{"key":"B","text":"witness"},{"key":"C","text":"observe"},{"key":"D","text":"approve"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"as the careers of their elites…___ 主语 careers 原文 as the __(12)__ of their elites, including several world-renowned scientists, __(13)__ 中，空 13 的主语是 the careers of their elites，as 引导'正如…所证实/所表明的'。线索指向'职业生涯能起到证实作用'的动词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"affirm='证实、断言'，可由 careers 这类抽象事实做主语，表'精英们的职业生涯证实了该群体的贡献'，与前句的论断形成证据链。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"witness='见证'时，主语典型是 the 20th century / Beijing 等时代地点；让 careers 'witness'不地道。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"observe 主语多为人，意为'观察、遵守'，不能由 careers 做主语'观察'某事。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"approve='批准、赞同'，主语通常为人或机构，且其'认可'与'印证贡献'是不同动作。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moreover"},{"key":"B","text":"therefore"},{"key":"C","text":"however"},{"key":"D","text":"meanwhile"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"14.","reason":"前两句并列了 IQ 高与遗传病多，下句却说'以前没人把它俩联系起来' 前文一句 does well in IQ test，另一句 They also suffer more often than most people from a number of nasty genetic diseases, such as breast cancer 列出两组事实；空所在句 These facts, __(14)__, have previously been thought unrelated 出现'These facts'回指，'have previously been thought unrelated'是与前文的'反差'——本应有联系的两件事一直被认为无关，逻辑转折。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"moreover 表递进添加，但本句是把前两组事实拉到对照面解释，是反转而非'更进一步说同向'。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"therefore 表'因此'，前两句并非'高 IQ 导致遗传病'或'遗传病导致 IQ 高'的因果关系，逻辑荒谬。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"however='然而'，与下文 have previously been thought unrelated 一起表明：尽管两组事实并列出现，但人们以前却一直把它们当作无关——为接下来 Cochran 把二者关联起来的新观点埋下转折伏笔。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"meanwhile='与此同时'多用于时间并列，无法表达'但此前却被认为无关'的对比。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"given up"},{"key":"B","text":"got over"},{"key":"C","text":"carried on"},{"key":"D","text":"put down"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"前者被归因于社会因素 原文 The former has been __(15)__ to social effects, such as a strong tradition of __(16)__ education——The former 指'高 IQ'这件事，过去一直被'归因于'社会因素（如重视教育的传统），空里要填的就是'归因于'之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"given up to='让位给/向…放弃'，逻辑上'前者被放弃给社会因素'不通顺，且文意是寻找解释，不是放弃。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"got over='克服、从…恢复'，宾语通常是病痛/困难，'高 IQ 被克服给社会因素'不成句。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"carried on='继续做'，不与 to 引导原因连用，搭配不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"put down 与 to 搭配为 put X down to Y='把 X 归因于 Y'，意为'高 IQ 此前被归因于社会因素，如重视教育的传统'，与下文 such as a strong tradition of __(16)__ education 列举的'原因'完美呼应。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assessing"},{"key":"B","text":"supervising"},{"key":"C","text":"administering"},{"key":"D","text":"valuing"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"用以解释'为何 IQ 高'的社会传统 原文 The former has been __(15)__ to social effects, such as a strong tradition of __(16)__ education——既然要解释高 IQ，那么这种'传统'应是促进/重视教育的传统；'重视教育'才能合理地与'IQ 高'对接。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assessing education='评估教育'是行政行为，不是一种解释族群高 IQ 的文化传统。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"supervising education='监督教育'是管理动作，与'文化传统重视'相去甚远。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"administering education='管理/施行教育'是行政性动作，与'群体性传统重视教育'语义脱节。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"valuing education='重视教育'，是该族群常被提到的文化传统，恰好可作'高 IQ'的社会解释，与上文 __(15)__ to social effects 的归因链对应。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"development"},{"key":"B","text":"origin"},{"key":"C","text":"consequence"},{"key":"D","text":"instrument"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"后者（遗传病）被视为基因隔离的结果 原文 The latter was seen as a (an) __(17)__ of genetic isolation——The latter 指'遗传病'。基因隔离（遗传上的封闭、近亲繁衍）会导致遗传病多发，是因果关系，遗传病是基因隔离的'后果'。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"development of='…的发展'，遗传病不是'基因隔离的发展'，逻辑不顺。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"origin of='…的起源'，意味着遗传病是基因隔离的起源，因果方向恰好反了：是基因隔离造成遗传病，不是相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"consequence of='…的结果'，遗传病是基因隔离的结果，与生物学常识与上下文一致；同时与 14 题 however、15 题 put down to 形成'旧解释体系'：高 IQ 归因社会，遗传病归因基因隔离。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"instrument of='…的工具'，遗传病不是基因隔离的工具，逻辑不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"linked"},{"key":"B","text":"integrated"},{"key":"C","text":"woven"},{"key":"D","text":"combined"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"Cochran 提出二者'密切相关' 原文 Dr. Cochran suggests that the intelligence and diseases are intimately __(18)__——Cochran 主张'智力和疾病紧密相连'，下一句 His argument is that the unusual history of these people has __(19)__ them to unique evolutionary pressures that have resulted in this __(20)__ state of affairs 进一步说明二者来源相同。'相联'是因果/统计上的关联，最自然的动词是 link。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"linked 与 intimately 形成 intimately linked='密切相连'，是科研论文中表'有内在联系'的标准搭配，且符合 Cochran 把二者关联到同一进化压力的论证目的。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"integrated 强调'融合为一体'，但智力与疾病不是被合并的两部分，而是同一进化过程的副产品。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"woven 多用于'编织进某事中'，比喻偏文学，且与 intimately 搭配在科研语体中不常见。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"combined 多用于物质或要素组合为新整体，描述两个独立现象之间的因果关联不如 link 自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"limited"},{"key":"B","text":"subjected"},{"key":"C","text":"converted"},{"key":"D","text":"directed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"19.","reason":"非凡历史使他们遭受独特进化压力 原文 the unusual history of these people has __(19)__ them to unique evolutionary pressures——历史让这些人'遭受'了独特的进化压力，意为他们被迫接受/经历了这些压力，最契合 subject to。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"limited them to=把他们限制在……，但'把他们限制到独特的进化压力上'不通顺，文意是经历而非限制。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"subjected them to unique evolutionary pressures='使他们遭受独特的进化压力'，精确对应'独特历史→独特进化压力'的因果链，并为下一句 resulted in this __(20)__ state of affairs 做铺垫。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"converted them to='把他们转变为'，多接结果状态（信仰/物质），把人转变为'进化压力'语义荒谬。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"directed them to='把他们引向…'，强调方向引导，但进化压力是'施加'而非'引导前往'，搭配不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"paradoxical"},{"key":"B","text":"incompatible"},{"key":"C","text":"inevitable"},{"key":"D","text":"continuous"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"智力与疾病同源、看似矛盾 全段从 They also suffer more often than most people from a number of nasty genetic diseases 摆出'高 IQ 与高发遗传病并存'的反差现象，到 the intelligence and diseases are intimately __(18)__ 揭示二者同源；这种'高智力与遗传病同时存在且彼此关联'的局面正是英语中的 paradox。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"paradoxical state of affairs='看似矛盾的局面'，紧扣全段反差——智力高（好）与遗传病多（坏）这两件看起来对立的事实却同源于一种进化压力，正是 paradox 的核心特征，且照应了文章开篇 dare not speak its name 那种'反常识'的张力。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"incompatible='不相容'，意味两者不能并存；但事实上二者在同一群体中并存，且 Cochran 把它们关联到同一原因，与 incompatible 的'不可共存'矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"inevitable='不可避免'，强调'必然如此'，但全文重点不在'必然性'，而在'看似矛盾而实有共因'的反常性。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"continuous='连续的、持续的'，是时间属性，与'高 IQ 与遗传病并存的反差'无直接关联。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"While still catching up to men in some spheres of modern life, women appear to be way ahead in at least one undesirable category. \"Women are particularly susceptible to developing depression and anxiety disorders in response to stress compared to men,\" according to Dr. Yehuda, chief psychiatrist at New York's Veteran's Administration Hospital."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Studies of both animals and humans have shown that sex hormones somehow affect the stress response, causing females under stress to produce more of the trigger chemicals than do males under the same conditions. In several of the studies, when stressed-out female rats had their ovaries (the female reproductive organs) removed, their chemical responses became equal to those of the males."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"Adding to a woman's increased dose of stress chemicals, are her increased \"opportunities\" for stress. \"It's not necessarily that women don't cope as well. It's just that they have so much more to cope with,\" says Dr. Yehuda. \"Their capacity for tolerating stress may even be greater than men's,\" she observes, \"it's just that they're dealing with so many more things that they become worn out from it more visibly and sooner.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Dr. Yehuda notes another difference between the sexes. \"I think that the kinds of things that women are exposed to tend to be in more of a chronic or repeated nature. Men go to war and are exposed to combat stress. Men are exposed to more acts of random physical violence. The kinds of interpersonal violence that women are exposed to tend to be in domestic situations, by, unfortunately, parents or other family members, and they tend not to be one-shot deals. The wear-and-tear that comes from these longer relationships can be quite devastating.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Adeline Alvarez married at 18 and gave birth to a son, but was determined to finish college. \"I struggled a lot to get the college degree. I was living in so much frustration that that was my escape, to go to school, and get ahead and do better.\" Later, her marriage ended and she became a single mother. \"It's the hardest thing to take care of a teenager, have a job, pay the rent, pay the car payment, and pay the debt. I lived from paycheck to paycheck.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"Not everyone experiences the kinds of severe chronic stresses Alvarez describes. But most women today are coping with a lot of obligations, with few breaks, and feeling the strain. Alvarez's experience demonstrates the importance of finding ways to diffuse stress before it threatens your health and your ability to function."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the first two paragraphs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Women are biologically more vulnerable to stress."},{"key":"B","text":"Women are still suffering much stress caused by men."},{"key":"C","text":"Women are more experienced than men in coping with stress."},{"key":"D","text":"Men and women show different inclinations when faced with stress."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据前两段，下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"女性在生理上更容易受到压力的影响。","B":"女性仍在遭受由男性造成的巨大压力。","C":"女性在应对压力方面比男性更有经验。","D":"男性和女性在面对压力时表现出不同的倾向。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干Which of the following is true according to the first two paragraphs?把范围锁死在前两段，又要求判断真伪，是典型的范围细节题。","parse":"主句省略be动词的Which of the following is true是个简单选择问句，难点只在状语according to the first two paragraphs——according to 在这里意为“依据……所述”，限定信息来源范围，不是“按照……行动”，无任何陷阱。","locateEn":"Studies of both animals and humans have shown that sex hormones somehow affect the stress response, causing females under stress to produce more of the trigger chemicals than do males under the same conditions.","locateZh":"针对动物和人类的多项研究表明，性激素会以某种方式影响压力反应，使得承受压力的雌性比同等条件下的雄性分泌更多触发性化学物质。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判要点“女性在生理层面对压力更易感”与biologically more vulnerable逐词对应：biologically=sex hormones 层面，more vulnerable=produce more trigger chemicals 的属性表达。","pairs":[{"orig":"sex hormones somehow affect the stress response, causing females under stress to produce more of the trigger chemicals than do males","opt":"Women are biologically more vulnerable to stress."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"前两段只谈“女性对压力反应更强的生理机制”，完全没有提到stress caused by men这种来源归因——是典型把后文第四段才出现的“家庭暴力施害者”读法提前塞进前两段。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文从头到尾说女性“更易受压力影响”，从未说她们more experienced ... in coping with stress（更善应对）——这是典型“与原文相反”。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"前两段只展示生理反应程度的差异（女性分泌更多触发化学物质），并未谈different inclinations（不同的应对倾向/方式），属于偷换概念。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Dr. Yehuda's research suggests that women____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"need extra doses of chemicals to handle stress."},{"key":"B","text":"have limited capacity for tolerating stress."},{"key":"C","text":"are more capable of avoiding stress."},{"key":"D","text":"are exposed to more stress."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Yehuda博士的研究表明女性____","choicesZh":{"A":"需要额外剂量的化学物质来应对压力。","B":"承受压力的能力有限。","C":"更有能力避免压力。","D":"暴露在更多压力之下。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干Dr. Yehuda's research suggests that women____要求补全 Yehuda 研究的结论，结论必在 Yehuda 引言中直接给出。","parse":"Dr. Yehuda's research suggests that women____是“主+谓+that 宾语从句”结构，需要补全的是从句的谓语部分。注意 suggests 此处是“表明、显示”之意，不是“建议”——这是熟词僻义高频考点。","locateEn":"Adding to a woman's increased dose of stress chemicals, are her increased \"opportunities\" for stress. \"It's not necessarily that women don't cope as well. It's just that they have so much more to cope with,\" says Dr. Yehuda.","locateZh":"在女性大剂量压力化学物质之外，她们还面临更多的压力“机会”。Yehuda 博士说：“并非女性应对得不好，只是她们要应对的事情多得多。”","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"need extra doses of chemicals to handle stress把原文中作为压力反应产物的 trigger chemicals 误读成女性“需要额外服用化学药剂”——既颠倒了化学物质的来源（内生而非外服），也凭空增加了 need to handle 的目的。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"have limited capacity for tolerating stress说女性耐受能力有限，与第三段Their capacity for tolerating stress may even be greater than men's完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"more capable of avoiding stress“更善于避免压力”在原文毫无依据；第三段明说女性“要应对的事更多”，根本谈不上“避免”。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要点是“数量更多”，四项里只有more stress在“量”上吻合，且 are exposed to 与原文“opportunities for stress”在被动承受的语义上一致，锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"they have so much more to cope with","opt":"are exposed to more stress."},{"orig":"her increased \"opportunities\" for stress","opt":"are exposed to more stress."}]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, the stress women confront tends to be____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"domestic and temporary."},{"key":"B","text":"irregular and violent."},{"key":"C","text":"durable and frequent."},{"key":"D","text":"trivial and random."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第4段，女性面临的压力往往是____","choicesZh":{"A":"家庭性的和暂时性的。","B":"不规律的和剧烈的。","C":"持久的和频繁的。","D":"琐碎的和随机的。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干the stress women confront tends to be____要求归纳女性所受压力的特征，第四段恰好给出 chronic、repeated 等形容词作答。","parse":"According to Paragraph 4, the stress women confront tends to be____中，women confront是省略关系代词 that/which 的定语从句修饰 stress，意为“女性所面对的压力”；tends to be 表“倾向于是、往往是”，引出对压力性质的描述。","locateEn":"I think that the kinds of things that women are exposed to tend to be in more of a chronic or repeated nature. ... The kinds of interpersonal violence that women are exposed to tend to be in domestic situations, by, unfortunately, parents or other family members, and they tend not to be one-shot deals.","locateZh":"我认为，女性所暴露的那类事情往往更具慢性或反复的性质。……女性所遭受的人际暴力往往发生在家庭情境之中——不幸的是，施暴者往往是父母或其他家庭成员，而且这些暴力往往不是一次性的事件。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"domestic and temporary里 domestic 对应domestic situations确实没错，但 temporary（暂时的）与原文 chronic（慢性的）正好相反——典型的“半对半错”误答。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"irregular and violent里 irregular（无规律的/偶发的）是原文形容男性所受暴力（random physical violence）的特征，被张冠李戴到女性头上。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判“长期+反复”对应durable and frequent的“持久+频繁”两个形容词，完全等值，锁定 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"chronic or repeated nature","opt":"durable and frequent."},{"orig":"they tend not to be one-shot deals","opt":"durable and frequent."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"trivial and random：trivial（琐碎的）原文未提，random（随机的）又是男性的特征，两个词都不属于女性所受压力。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"The sentence \"I lived from paycheck to paycheck.\" (Line 6, Para. 5) shows that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Alvarez cared about nothing but making money."},{"key":"B","text":"Alvarez's salary barely covered her household expenses."},{"key":"C","text":"Alvarez got paychecks from different jobs."},{"key":"D","text":"Alvarez paid practically everything by check."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"句子\"我靠薪水勉强度日。\"(第5段第6行)表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"Alvarez除了赚钱什么都不关心。","B":"Alvarez的薪水勉强够支付她的家庭开支。","C":"Alvarez从不同的工作中获得薪水。","D":"Alvarez几乎所有东西都用支票支付。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干The sentence \"I lived from paycheck to paycheck.\" (Line 6, Para. 5) shows that____要求解读某句话“表明”了什么，正是典型句意题。","parse":"题干主干是The sentence ... shows that____，其中嵌套的I lived from paycheck to paycheck.是一个英语习语：from paycheck to paycheck 字面“从一份工资到下一份工资”，引申为“每月薪水刚好维持开销、毫无结余”——这是本题的全部语义负担。","locateEn":"It's the hardest thing to take care of a teenager, have a job, pay the rent, pay the car payment, and pay the debt. I lived from paycheck to paycheck.","locateZh":"照顾一个青少年、做一份工作、付房租、付车贷、还债——这是最难的事。我那时是月光族，每张工资都刚刚够用。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"cared about nothing but making money把“她拼命挣钱付账”扭曲为“除了挣钱什么都不在乎”——既忽视了她was determined to finish college的求学执念，也凭空给主人公贴上“功利”的负面标签。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判“工资刚好够支出”既匹配习语字面，又匹配前句开支清单——选项 B 用 barely covered + household expenses 把这两层信息全包了，唯一答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"pay the rent, pay the car payment, and pay the debt","opt":"Alvarez's salary barely covered her household expenses."},{"orig":"I lived from paycheck to paycheck.","opt":"Alvarez's salary barely covered her household expenses."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"got paychecks from different jobs把 from paycheck to paycheck 错读为“工资来自不同工作”——这是对习语的字面误解，原文从未说她有多份工作。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"paid practically everything by check把 paycheck（工资支票）扭成 by check（用支票付款）的支付方式——这是把“收到的工资”和“用支票付账”两件事偷换。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Strain of Stress: No Way Out?"},{"key":"B","text":"Responses to Stress: Gender Difference"},{"key":"C","text":"Stress Analysis: What Chemicals Say"},{"key":"D","text":"Gender Inequality: Women Under Stress"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"下列哪项最适合作为本文的标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"压力的重负:无路可走?","B":"对压力的反应:性别差异","C":"压力分析:化学物质说明了什么","D":"性别不平等:压力之下的女性"},"analysis":{"type":"题干Which of the following would be the best title for the text?要求选最佳标题，标准的主旨题问法。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?是简单选择问句，would 表“在这四个候选中最合适”的虚拟选择语气，无理解陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Strain of Stress: No Way Out?主语只剩 Stress，把“女性”这个全文真正主角丢了；副标题No Way Out?又抛出“无路可走”的悲观反问——尾段明明说the importance of finding ways to diffuse stress要寻找化解之道，态度并不绝望。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Responses to Stress: Gender Difference把全文重心定在“两性都受压力、各有差异”的对比框架，但文章只详细写女性这一边、男性仅作参照——并不是平起平坐的比较研究。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Stress Analysis: What Chemicals Say把视角锁死在“化学物质分析”这一第二段的局部点上，完全不覆盖第三、四、五、六段中关于社会、家庭、案例的内容——典型的“以偏概全”。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文主角始终是 women（生理更敏感、机会更多、受家庭暴力更久、案例又是 Alvarez），合格标题必须以 women 为中心；D 项把 Women 放在主标位、Gender Inequality 作角度，最贴合主线。","pairs":[{"orig":"Women are particularly susceptible to developing depression and anxiety disorders in response to stress","opt":"Gender Inequality: Women Under Stress"},{"orig":"most women today are coping with a lot of obligations, with few breaks, and feeling the strain","opt":"Gender Inequality: Women Under Stress"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"It used to be so straightforward. A team of researchers working together in the laboratory would submit the results of their research to a journal. A journal editor would then remove the authors' names and affiliations from the paper and send it to their peers for review. Depending on the comments received, the editor would accept the paper for publication or decline it. Copyright rested with the journal publisher, and researchers seeking knowledge of the results would have to subscribe to the journal."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"No longer. The Internet – and pressure from funding agencies, who are questioning why commercial publishers are making money from government-funded research by restricting access to it – is making free access to scientific results a reality. The Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) has just issued a report describing the far-reaching consequences of this. The report, by John Houghton of Victoria University in Australia and Graham Vickery of the OECD, makes heavy reading for publishers who have, so far, made handsome profits. But it goes further than that. It signals a change in what has, until now, been a key element of scientific endeavour."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"The value of knowledge and the return on the public investment in research depend, in part, upon wide distribution and ready access. It is big business. In America, the core scientific publishing market is estimated at between $7 billion and $11 billion. The International Association of Scientific, Technical and Medical Publishers says that there are more than 2,000 publishers worldwide specializing in these subjects. They publish more than 1.2 million articles each year in some 16,000 journals."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"This is now changing. According to the OECD report, some 75% of scholarly journals are now online. Entirely new business models are emerging; three main ones were identified by the report's authors. There is the so-called big deal, where institutional subscribers pay for access to a collection of online journal titles through site-licensing agreements. There is open-access publishing, typically supported by asking the author (or his employer) to pay for the paper to be published. Finally, there are open-access archives, where organizations such as universities or international laboratories support institutional repositories. Other models exist that are hybrids of these three, such as delayed open-access, where journals allow only subscribers to read a paper for the first six months, before making it freely available to everyone who wishes to see it. All this could change the traditional form of the peer-review process, at least for the publication of papers."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"In the first paragraph, the author discusses____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the background information of journal editing."},{"key":"B","text":"the publication routine of laboratory reports."},{"key":"C","text":"the relations of authors with journal publishers."},{"key":"D","text":"the traditional process of journal publication."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"在第一段中，作者讨论了____","choicesZh":{"A":"期刊编辑的背景信息","B":"实验室报告的出版惯例","C":"作者与期刊出版商的关系","D":"期刊出版的传统流程"},"analysis":{"type":"题干In the first paragraph, the author discusses____问的是整个第一段在讨论什么，属于\"段落主旨\"。","parse":"题干In the first paragraph, the author discusses____结构平直：In the first paragraph作状语，the author为主语，discusses为谓语，空格处填宾语。无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the background information of journal editing只覆盖了P1中编辑送审、决定刊用这一中段动作，不涵盖投稿、版权、订阅等环节。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"laboratory reports偷换原文submit the results of their research to a journal——研究成果以论文形式投稿期刊，与\"实验报告\"不是一回事；且原文讲的是出版流程，不是\"实验报告的发表惯例\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the relations of authors with journal publishers只截取作者与出版商的关系层面，遗漏编辑、评议者、读者等其他参与方，且\"关系\"不能涵盖整套\"流程\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D项traditional与used to对应、process与整段动作链对应、journal publication覆盖从投稿到读者获取——是对P1主旨的精准概括。","pairs":[{"orig":"It used to be so straightforward.","opt":"the traditional process of journal publication"},{"orig":"submit the results of their research to a journal","opt":"process of journal publication"}]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"Which of the following is true of the OECD report?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It criticizes government-funded research."},{"key":"B","text":"It introduces an effective means of publication."},{"key":"C","text":"It upsets profit-making journal publishers."},{"key":"D","text":"It benefits scientific research considerably."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于OECD报告，下列哪项是正确的？","choicesZh":{"A":"它批评了政府资助的研究","B":"它引入了一种有效的出版方式","C":"它使营利性期刊出版商感到不安","D":"它极大地有益于科学研究"},"analysis":{"type":"题干Which of the following is true of the OECD report?问关于OECD报告的哪项陈述为真，是典型\"四项中找一项与原文相符\"。","parse":"题干Which of the following is true of the OECD report?为which引导的疑问句，of the OECD report是后置定语修饰following。无陷阱。","locateEn":"The report, by John Houghton of Victoria University in Australia and Graham Vickery of the OECD, makes heavy reading for publishers who have, so far, made handsome profits.","locateZh":"这份由澳大利亚维多利亚大学的John Houghton和OECD的Graham Vickery撰写的报告，让那些迄今为止赚得盆满钵满的出版商读来颇为难受。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"criticizes government-funded research把行为主体张冠李戴——原文是funding agencies, who are questioning why commercial publishers are making money from government-funded research，质疑的是资助机构、对象是商业出版商限制访问，而非OECD报告批评政府资助研究。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"introduces an effective means of publication在P2找不到对应——P2只说报告描述了\"深远影响\"，没说它\"介绍了一种有效的出版手段\"；新出版模式的介绍在P4，且不是OECD报告的内容定位。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C把\"使...读来沉重\"换成upset、把\"一直赚高利润的\"压缩成profit-making，两个语义点全部落地，是定位句的标准同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"makes heavy reading for publishers","opt":"It upsets profit-making journal publishers"},{"orig":"publishers who have, so far, made handsome profits","opt":"profit-making journal publishers"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"It benefits scientific research considerably是从\"免费获取有利于科研\"这一常识做的延伸推断；但P2只说报告\"描述深远影响\"\"让出版商难受\"，并未直接评价它\"对科研有重大裨益\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"According to the text, online publication is significant in that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"it provides an easier access to scientific results."},{"key":"B","text":"it brings huge profits to scientific researchers."},{"key":"C","text":"it emphasizes the crucial role of scientific knowledge."},{"key":"D","text":"it facilitates public investment in scientific research."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章，在线出版的重要意义在于____","choicesZh":{"A":"它提供了获取科研成果的更便捷途径","B":"它为科研人员带来巨额利润","C":"它强调了科学知识的关键作用","D":"它促进了公众对科研的投资"},"analysis":{"type":"题干online publication is significant in that____中in that=因为，问online出版\"重要在哪一点\"，答案在原文中以陈述形式给出。","parse":"题干According to the text, online publication is significant in that____中According to the text是状语，online publication为主语，is significant是系表，in that____引导原因状语从句（in that=because）。","locateEn":"Other models exist that are hybrids of these three, such as delayed open-access, where journals allow only subscribers to read a paper for the first six months, before making it freely available to everyone who wishes to see it.","locateZh":"还存在这三种模式的混合体，比如\"延迟开放获取\"：期刊只允许订阅者在论文发表后的前六个月内阅读，六个月之后就向所有想看的人免费开放。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A把\"使免费获取成现实\"转写为\"提供更易获取\"——free是easier的子集（既免费又便利），是原文同义概念的轻微弱化，符合细节题正确项形态。","pairs":[{"orig":"making free access to scientific results a reality","opt":"provides an easier access to scientific results"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"brings huge profits to scientific researchers把利润归给研究者；原文中赚钱的是publishers who have, so far, made handsome profits——出版商，且文章主线恰恰是\"在线/免费访问正在终结出版商的利润\"，正好与B相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"emphasizes the crucial role of scientific knowledge答的是\"在线出版强调了科学知识的关键作用\"——文章虽提及知识价值（P3首句），但那是泛论，不是online publication的significance。题干问的是online的价值，C跳到了\"知识的价值\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"facilitates public investment in scientific research说\"网络出版促进了对科研的公共投资\"；原文只说\"知识价值与公共投资的回报取决于广泛传播\"（P3），并未说在线出版反过来促进了投资本身。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"With the open-access publishing model, the author of a paper is required to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cover the cost of its publication."},{"key":"B","text":"subscribe to the journal publishing it."},{"key":"C","text":"allow other online journals to use it freely."},{"key":"D","text":"complete the peer-review before submission."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在开放获取出版模式下，论文作者需要____","choicesZh":{"A":"支付其出版费用","B":"订阅刊登该论文的期刊","C":"允许其他在线期刊免费使用该论文","D":"在提交前完成同行评审"},"analysis":{"type":"题干the author of a paper is required to____问\"被要求做什么\"，是对原文中一句陈述的复述式考查。","parse":"题干With the open-access publishing model, the author of a paper is required to____：With短语作状语限定模式范围，the author of a paper为主语，is required to____为被动结构，空格处填动词原形。","locateEn":"There is open-access publishing, typically supported by asking the author (or his employer) to pay for the paper to be published.","locateZh":"还有开放获取出版模式，通常是要求作者（或其雇主）为论文的发表付费来支持运转。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A把\"付费让论文发表\"转写为\"承担发表成本\"，含义完全等值——是定位句动作的标准同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"asking the author (or his employer) to pay for the paper to be published","opt":"cover the cost of its publication"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"subscribe to the journal publishing it描述的是P1的旧模式（researchers seeking knowledge of the results would have to subscribe to the journal），恰是open-access要推翻的对象，与新模式完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"allow other online journals to use it freely在P4找不到对应——open-access强调读者免费获取，未要求作者授权其他期刊免费使用其论文。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"complete the peer-review before submission在P4找不到对应——P4末句说All this could change the traditional form of the peer-review process，是说同行评议形式会变，但未要求作者投稿前自行完成评议。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"Which of the following best summarizes the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The Internet is posing a threat to publishers."},{"key":"B","text":"A new mode of publication is emerging."},{"key":"C","text":"Authors welcome the new channel for publication."},{"key":"D","text":"Publication is rendered easier by online service."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"下列哪项最好地概括了本文？","choicesZh":{"A":"互联网正在对出版商构成威胁","B":"一种新的出版模式正在兴起","C":"作者们欢迎这种新的出版渠道","D":"在线服务使出版变得更加容易"},"analysis":{"type":"题干Which of the following best summarizes the text?让从四项中选最能概括全文的一项，是典型全文主旨题。","parse":"题干Which of the following best summarizes the text?为which引导的特殊疑问句，best summarizes为谓语，the text为宾语。结构平直无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"The Internet is posing a threat to publishers只抓住P2中\"让出版商难受\"这一局部，没覆盖P4新模式群的描述与P1旧模式的对照；且文章并非以\"威胁出版商\"为主线，而是以\"模式更替\"为主线。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B用\"new mode of publication is emerging\"一句概括了P1旧模式、P2转折、P3铺垫、P4新模式群——覆盖每一段，是全文主旨的精准提炼。","pairs":[{"orig":"Entirely new business models are emerging","opt":"A new mode of publication is emerging"},{"orig":"No longer.","opt":"A new mode of publication is emerging"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Authors welcome the new channel for publication说作者欢迎新出版渠道；原文从头到尾未表达作者群体的态度，文中讨论的是\"模式更替\"本身，不是作者群体的情感反应。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Publication is rendered easier by online service只抓\"在线让出版更容易\"这一局部影响，没覆盖三种新模式、传统模式式微、市场规模等全文要点；且原文重心是\"模式更替\"，不是\"更容易出版\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"In the early 1960s Wilt Chamberlain was one of the only three players in the National Basketball Association (NBA) listed at over seven feet. If he had played last season, however, he would have been one of 42. The bodies playing major professional sports have changed dramatically over the years, and managers have been more than willing to adjust team uniforms to fit the growing numbers of bigger, longer frames."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The trend in sports, though, may be obscuring an unrecognized reality: Americans have generally stopped growing. Though typically about two inches taller now than 140 years ago, today's people – especially those born to families who have lived in the U.S. for many generations – apparently reached their limit in the early 1960s. And they aren't likely to get any taller. \"In the general population today, at this genetic, environmental level, we've pretty much gone as far as we can go,\" says anthropologist William Cameron Chumlea of Wright State University. In the case of NBA players, their increase in height appears to result from the increasingly common practice of recruiting players from all over the world."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Growth, which rarely continues beyond the age of 20, demands calories and nutrients – notably, protein – to feed expanding tissues. At the start of the 20th century, under-nutrition and childhood infections got in the way. But as diet and health improved, children and adolescents have, on average, increased in height by about an inch and a half every 20 years, a pattern known as the secular trend in height. Yet according to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, average height – 5′9″ for men, 5′4″ for women – hasn't really changed since 1960."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Genetically speaking, there are advantages to avoiding substantial height. During childbirth, larger babies have more difficulty passing through the birth canal. Moreover, even though humans have been upright for millions of years, our feet and back continue to struggle with bipedal posture and cannot easily withstand repeated strain imposed by oversize limbs. \"There are some real constraints that are set by the genetic architecture of the individual organism,\" says anthropologist William Leonard of Northwestern University."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"Genetic maximums can change, but don't expect this to happen soon. Claire C. Gordon, senior anthropologist at the Army Research Center in Natick, Mass., ensures that 90 percent of the uniforms and workstations fit recruits without alteration. She says that, unlike those for basketball, the length of military uniforms has not changed for some time. And if you need to predict human height in the near future to design a piece of equipment, Gordon says that by and large, \"you could use today's data and feel fairly confident.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"Wilt Chamberlain is cited as an example to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"illustrate the change of height of NBA players."},{"key":"B","text":"show the popularity of NBA players in the U.S."},{"key":"C","text":"compare different generations of NBA players."},{"key":"D","text":"assess the achievements of famous NBA players."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"引用Wilt Chamberlain作为例子是为了____","choicesZh":{"A":"说明NBA球员身高的变化。","B":"展示NBA球员在美国的受欢迎程度。","C":"比较不同时代的NBA球员。","D":"评估著名NBA球员的成就。"},"analysis":{"type":"cited as an example to 这个短语直白告诉考生：问的是举此例的目的、即作者用它来支持哪个论点。","parse":"Wilt Chamberlain is cited as an example to____ 是被动结构，主语 Wilt Chamberlain 是被引用的对象，真正的施动者是文章作者；不定式 to____ 表目的，需要在选项里补一个动词短语，回答\"作者引用他来做什么\"。结构平直无陷阱。","locateEn":"In the early 1960s Wilt Chamberlain was one of the only three players in the National Basketball Association (NBA) listed at over seven feet. If he had played last season, however, he would have been one of 42. The bodies playing major professional sports have changed dramatically over the years.","locateZh":"上世纪60年代初，威尔特·张伯伦是 NBA 中仅有的三位身高超七英尺的球员之一。可若他在上赛季打球，他会是 42 位这样的球员之一。多年来，从事重大职业体育的运动员的体型已经发生了戏剧性变化。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"示范身高在变\"与 illustrate the change of height of NBA players 一一对应，作者举张伯伦正是为了让\"3 人→42 人\"的身高对比说话。","pairs":[{"orig":"The bodies playing major professional sports have changed dramatically over the years","opt":"illustrate the change of height of NBA players"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 show the popularity of NBA players in the U.S. 中 popularity 一词在 P1 乃至全文都没有出现，作者也未谈 NBA 球员是否受欢迎，是凭印象添加。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P1 只把张伯伦时代与上赛季两个时间点的球员数量做对比，并未拿出多代 NBA 球员逐代相较；选项 compare different generations of NBA players 把\"对比身高数据\"偷换成\"代际比较\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"P1 通篇不评张伯伦或其他球员的篮球成就，仅用其身高数据做例子；选项 assess the achievements of famous NBA players 答非所问。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"Which of the following plays a key role in body growth according to the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Genetic modification."},{"key":"B","text":"Natural environment."},{"key":"C","text":"Living standards."},{"key":"D","text":"Daily exercise."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,以下哪一项在身体生长中起关键作用?","choicesZh":{"A":"基因改造。","B":"自然环境。","C":"生活水平。","D":"日常锻炼。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following plays a key role in body growth according to the text? 是 which 引导的事实判断，问\"根据原文，哪一项起关键作用\"，要求直接到文中找事实陈述，属典型细节题。","parse":"Which of the following plays a key role in body growth according to the text? 主干 Which plays a key role，which 作主语；介词短语 in body growth 限定范围，according to the text 限定依据来源。无难点。","locateEn":"Growth, which rarely continues beyond the age of 20, demands calories and nutrients – notably, protein – to feed expanding tissues. At the start of the 20th century, under-nutrition and childhood infections got in the way. But as diet and health improved, children and adolescents have, on average, increased in height by about an inch and a half every 20 years, a pattern known as the secular trend in height.","locateZh":"生长——通常不会延续到 20 岁以后——需要热量与营养（尤其是蛋白质）来供养扩张中的组织。20 世纪初，营养不良与儿童期感染挡住了路。但随着饮食和健康的改善，儿童和青少年的平均身高每 20 年增加约一英寸半，这一规律被称作\"身高的世俗增长趋势\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P4 反而说基因 constraints 限制了进一步长高，从未把 Genetic modification（基因改造）当成长高原因；Genetic modification 在文中既不存在也与文意相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"at this genetic, environmental level 仅一笔带过 environmental，并未把\"自然环境\"立为身高增长的关键因素；真正被原文展开论证的是饮食/健康，而非自然环境。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"把饮食、营养、健康打包升一级，得到\"生活水平\"，与 Living standards. 完全等值，故选 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"as diet and health improved, children and adolescents have, on average, increased in height by about an inch and a half every 20 years","opt":"Living standards."},{"orig":"calories and nutrients","opt":"Living standards."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文谈到生长的条件只有 calories and nutrients 与 diet and health，从未涉及 Daily exercise，属常识硬塞。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"On which of the following statements would the author most probably agree?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Non-Americans add to the average height of the nation."},{"key":"B","text":"Human height is conditioned by the upright posture."},{"key":"C","text":"Americans are the tallest on average in the world."},{"key":"D","text":"Larger babies tend to become taller in adulthood."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者最可能同意以下哪一种说法?","choicesZh":{"A":"非美国人增加了国家的平均身高。","B":"人类身高受直立姿势的制约。","C":"美国人的平均身高是世界上最高的。","D":"体型较大的婴儿成年后往往更高。"},"analysis":{"type":"On which of the following statements would the author most probably agree? 用 most probably agree 询问作者最可能赞同的命题，没有给出明确定位词，要求四选项逐项回原文比对，是推断题特征。","parse":"On which of the following statements would the author most probably agree? 是 on which 前置的疑问句，正常语序应为 The author would most probably agree on which of the following statements——介词 on 与 agree 搭配，对薄弱考生可能造成结构错觉。","locateEn":"Moreover, even though humans have been upright for millions of years, our feet and back continue to struggle with bipedal posture and cannot easily withstand repeated strain imposed by oversize limbs.","locateZh":"而且，尽管人类已经直立行走了数百万年，我们的脚和背依然在与双足姿势苦战，难以承受来自过长肢体反复施加的劳损。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"In the case of NBA players, their increase in height appears to result from the increasingly common practice of recruiting players from all over the world. 只解释 NBA 球员变高的特殊原因，并未涉及\"非美籍人士拉高了全美平均身高\"——文中明确强调 Americans have generally stopped growing。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"脚与背承受不住超长肢体的劳损，就意味着\"长得太高\"会与直立姿势冲突，故\"身高受直立姿势制约\"正是作者立场。","pairs":[{"orig":"our feet and back continue to struggle with bipedal posture and cannot easily withstand repeated strain imposed by oversize limbs","opt":"Human height is conditioned by the upright posture."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只给美国数据 5′9″ for men, 5′4″ for women 和增长趋势，未与任何其他国家比较；tallest on average in the world 完全无据。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"During childbirth, larger babies have more difficulty passing through the birth canal. 把 larger babies 与生育困难联系，并未给出\"大宝宝长大会更高\"的因果；选项与原文反向偷推。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"We learn from the last paragraph that in the near future____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the garment industry will reconsider the uniform size."},{"key":"B","text":"the design of military uniforms will remain unchanged."},{"key":"C","text":"genetic testing will be employed in selecting sportsmen."},{"key":"D","text":"the existing data of human height will still be applicable."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从最后一段我们了解到,在不久的将来____","choicesZh":{"A":"服装业将重新考虑统一尺码。","B":"军装的设计将保持不变。","C":"基因检测将被用于选拔运动员。","D":"现有的人类身高数据仍将适用。"},"analysis":{"type":"We learn from the last paragraph that in the near future____ 中 we learn from 表明信息直接源自原文段，要求复述段中事实，不需多步推理，是细节题。","parse":"We learn from the last paragraph that in the near future____ that 引导宾语从句，从句被四个选项分别补全；in the near future 是从句的时间状语，提示选项应描述未来情形。","locateEn":"She says that, unlike those for basketball, the length of military uniforms has not changed for some time. And if you need to predict human height in the near future to design a piece of equipment, Gordon says that by and large, \"you could use today's data and feel fairly confident.\"","locateZh":"她说，和篮球队服不同，军服的长度已经很久没改过了。如果你需要在不久的将来预测人体身高来设计某种装备，Gordon 说，总的来说，\"你完全可以用今天的数据，并对此相当有信心\"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P5 仅讲 Gordon 所在的陆军研究中心和\"军服长度未变\"，根本没提服装产业是否会重审尺码；the garment industry will reconsider 无中生有。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the length of military uniforms has not changed for some time 是描述过去到现在的事实，并未承诺未来必然不变；will remain unchanged 把过去事实当成未来保证。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P5 谈装备设计与身高预测，与基因检测选拔运动员无关；genetic testing 在末段没有任何对应。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Gordon 明确表态短期内身高基本不变，故现存数据仍然有效，D 项是对她结论的标准转述。","pairs":[{"orig":"you could use today's data and feel fairly confident","opt":"the existing data of human height will still be applicable"}]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"The text intends to tell us that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the change of human height follows a cyclic pattern."},{"key":"B","text":"human height is becoming even more predictable."},{"key":"C","text":"Americans have reached their genetic growth limit."},{"key":"D","text":"the genetic pattern of Americans has altered."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"本文旨在告诉我们____","choicesZh":{"A":"人类身高的变化遵循周期性模式。","B":"人类身高正变得更加可预测。","C":"美国人已经达到了他们的遗传生长极限。","D":"美国人的基因模式已经改变。"},"analysis":{"type":"The text intends to tell us that____ 整句关心的是作者写整篇文章的总意图，是统摄全文的主旨问法。","parse":"The text intends to tell us that____ 主语 the text 被拟人化（实际指作者）；动词 intends to tell 是\"打算告诉\"，that 引导待补全的宾语从句。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P3 描述的是\"持续上升后趋平\"的单向曲线，并未提到任何循环涨跌；cyclic pattern 无据。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"you could use today's data and feel fairly confident 只是末段一处细节，且并非\"越来越可预测\"——原文表达是\"已经稳定可用\"，不是\"更可预测\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P2 转折立靶 + P5 重申结论，全篇围绕\"基因身高上限已被触及\"展开，C 项是最大公约数。","pairs":[{"orig":"we've pretty much gone as far as we can go","opt":"Americans have reached their genetic growth limit."},{"orig":"Genetic maximums can change, but don't expect this to happen soon.","opt":"Americans have reached their genetic growth limit."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"we've pretty much gone as far as we can go 与 Genetic maximums can change, but don't expect this to happen soon 都强调\"基因模式没变也不会很快变\"；has altered 与原文方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"In 1784, five years before he became president of the United States, George Washington, 52, was nearly toothless. So he hired a dentist to transplant nine teeth into his jaw – having extracted them from the mouths of his slaves."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"That's a far different image from the cherry-tree-chopping George most people remember from their history books. But recently, many historians have begun to focus on the role slavery played in the lives of the founding generation. They have been spurred in part by DNA evidence made available in 1998, which almost certainly proved Thomas Jefferson had fathered at least one child with his slave Sally Hemings. And only over the past 30 years have scholars examined history from the bottom up. Works of several historians reveal the moral compromises made by the nation's early leaders and the fragile nature of the country's infancy. More significantly, they argue that many of the Founding Fathers knew slavery was wrong – and yet most did little to fight it."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"More than anything, the historians say, the founders were hampered by the culture of their time. While Washington and Jefferson privately expressed distaste for slavery, they also understood that it was part of the political and economic bedrock of the country they helped to create."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"For one thing, the South could not afford to part with its slaves. Owning slaves was \"like having a large bank account,\" says Wiencek, author of An Imperfect God: George Washington, His Slaves, and the Creation of America. The southern states would not have signed the Constitution without protections for the \"peculiar institution,\" including a clause that counted a slave as three fifths of a man for purposes of congressional representation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"And the statesmen's political lives depended on slavery. The three-fifths formula handed Jefferson his narrow victory in the presidential election of 1800 by inflating the votes of the southern states in the Electoral College. Once in office, Jefferson extended slavery with the Louisiana Purchase in 1803; the new land was carved into 13 states, including three slave states."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"Still, Jefferson freed Hemings's children – though not Hemings herself or his approximately 150 other slaves. Washington, who had begun to believe that all men were created equal after observing the bravery of the black soldiers during the Revolutionary War, overcame the strong opposition of his relatives to grant his slaves their freedom in his will. Only a decade earlier, such an act would have required legislative approval in Virginia."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"George Washington's dental surgery is mentioned to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"show the primitive medical practice in the past."},{"key":"B","text":"demonstrate the cruelty of slavery in his days."},{"key":"C","text":"stress the role of slaves in the U.S. history."},{"key":"D","text":"reveal some unknown aspect of his life."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"提到乔治·华盛顿的牙科手术是为了____","choicesZh":{"A":"展示过去原始的医疗实践。","B":"证明他那个时代奴隶制的残酷。","C":"强调奴隶在美国历史中的作用。","D":"揭示他生活中一些不为人知的方面。"},"analysis":{"type":"is mentioned to 直接问\"提及某事的目的\"，是例证目的题的标准句式。","parse":"Q36 是一个被动语态加不定式的不完整陈述，is mentioned to 后接选项构成完整句子，主干就是 \"dental surgery is mentioned to do something\"，结构平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"In 1784, five years before he became president of the United States, George Washington, 52, was nearly toothless. So he hired a dentist to transplant nine teeth into his jaw – having extracted them from the mouths of his slaves.","locateZh":"1784 年，距他成为美国总统还有五年，52 岁的乔治·华盛顿几乎掉光了牙齿。于是他雇了一名牙医，往自己的下颌里移植了九颗牙——这些牙是从他奴隶们的嘴里拔出来的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 show the primitive medical practice in the past 拿\"用奴隶的牙做移植\"硬推\"医学原始\"，但原文从未对这桩手术作医学水平上的评价，作者关心的是\"牙齿来源\"而非\"医术水平\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 demonstrate the cruelty of slavery in his days 把\"从奴隶口中拔牙\"直接等同于\"展示奴隶制残酷\"，但作者紧接的评论句 That's a far different image 强调的是华盛顿形象的反差，而不是奴隶制残酷的程度。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 stress the role of slaves in the U.S. history 看似与第二段后文 the role slavery played 呼应，但作者讲牙科故事的直接目的是反差华盛顿形象，\"奴隶在历史中扮演的角色\"是更宏观的话题，由第二段后半句承担，不是牙科例子的直接服务对象。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"揭示鲜为人知的一面\"与 reveal some unknown aspect of his life 在语义上完全重合，直接锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"That's a far different image from the cherry-tree-chopping George most people remember from their history books","opt":"reveal some unknown aspect of his life"}]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"We may infer from the second paragraph that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"DNA technology has been widely applied to history research."},{"key":"B","text":"in its early days the U.S. was confronted with delicate situations."},{"key":"C","text":"historians deliberately made up some stories of Jefferson's life."},{"key":"D","text":"political compromises are easily found throughout the U.S. history."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第二段我们可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"DNA技术已被广泛应用于历史研究。","B":"美国在早期面临着微妙的局面。","C":"历史学家故意编造了一些Jefferson生平的故事。","D":"政治妥协在美国历史中很容易找到。"},"analysis":{"type":"We may infer from the second paragraph that 是推断题的标准措辞。","parse":"Q37 主干 \"We may infer that ...\"，from 介词短语限定推断的来源段落，结构清晰、无理解障碍。","locateEn":"Works of several historians reveal the moral compromises made by the nation's early leaders and the fragile nature of the country's infancy.","locateZh":"几位历史学家的著作揭示了这个国家早期领导人所做的道德妥协，以及国家初创期的脆弱性质。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 DNA technology has been widely applied to history research 中的 \"widely\"（广泛地）无原文依据；原文 DNA evidence made available in 1998, which almost certainly proved Thomas Jefferson 只是举出 DNA 用于杰斐逊一例，不能推出\"广泛应用于历史研究\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"由预判\"初期处境微妙\"对照四个选项，只有 B 用 delicate situations 完整捕捉 fragile nature 的语义，锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"the fragile nature of the country's infancy","opt":"in its early days the U.S. was confronted with delicate situations"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 historians deliberately made up some stories of Jefferson's life 中的 \"made up\"（编造）与原文 almost certainly proved（几乎确凿地证明）方向完全相反——原文说 DNA 证明了杰斐逊确有此事，并非历史学家凭空编造。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 political compromises are easily found throughout the U.S. history 把 the nation's early leaders 的\"早期\"扩张到 throughout the U.S. history 的\"整个美国历史\"；原文谈的只是国父们的妥协，不能推及整个美国史。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"What do we learn about Thomas Jefferson?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"His political view changed his attitude towards slavery."},{"key":"B","text":"His status as a father made him free the child slaves."},{"key":"C","text":"His attitude towards slavery was complex."},{"key":"D","text":"His affair with a slave stained his prestige."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于Thomas Jefferson我们了解到什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"他的政治观点改变了他对奴隶制的态度。","B":"他作为父亲的身份使他释放了儿童奴隶。","C":"他对奴隶制的态度是复杂的。","D":"他与一名奴隶的私情玷污了他的声望。"},"analysis":{"type":"What do we learn about Thomas Jefferson? 问\"我们了解到关于他的什么\"，要求归纳与他直接相关的全部事实陈述。","parse":"Q38 是简单特殊疑问句 What ... about X，结构无修饰从句，无陷阱。","locateEn":"More significantly, they argue that many of the Founding Fathers knew slavery was wrong – and yet most did little to fight it.","locateZh":"更意味深长的是，他们指出，许多开国元勋明知奴隶制是错的——然而他们中的大多数人却几乎没有为反对它做过什么。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 His political view changed his attitude towards slavery 提出\"政治观改变了他对奴隶制的态度\"，但全文没有任何句子说杰斐逊\"改变了\"态度——他的私下反感与公开扩张是同时存在的两面，不是先后转变。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 His status as a father made him free the child slaves 把杰斐逊解放 Hemings 孩子的行为归因于\"父亲身份\"，但原文 Jefferson freed Hemings's children 只陈述事实，未交代动机；选项把\"父亲身份\"作为驱动力，是凭常识强加的因果。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"杰斐逊在文中分别表现出反感、扩张、部分释放三种相互冲突的取向，唯有 complex 能把这三股力量都装下；其余选项最多只能解释其中一面。","pairs":[{"orig":"Jefferson privately expressed distaste for slavery","opt":"His attitude towards slavery was complex"},{"orig":"Jefferson extended slavery with the Louisiana Purchase in 1803; the new land was carved into 13 states, including three slave states","opt":"His attitude towards slavery was complex"},{"orig":"Jefferson freed Hemings's children – though not Hemings herself or his approximately 150 other slaves","opt":"His attitude towards slavery was complex"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 His affair with a slave stained his prestige 中的 stained his prestige（玷污了他的声望）在原文找不到任何评价依据；P2 只说 DNA 证明了亲子关系，并未评价此事对他声望的影响。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Some Founding Fathers benefit politically from slavery."},{"key":"B","text":"Slaves in the old days did not have the right to vote."},{"key":"C","text":"Slaves owners usually had large savings accounts."},{"key":"D","text":"Slavery was regarded as a peculiar institution."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"一些开国元勋在政治上从奴隶制中获益。","B":"旧时代的奴隶没有投票权。","C":"奴隶主通常有大量的储蓄账户。","D":"奴隶制被视为一种特殊的制度。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true according to the text? 判断哪一项符合原文事实，本质是细节核对。","parse":"Q39 主干 \"Which is true according to the text\"，无从句、无否定，结构平铺直叙。","locateEn":"And the statesmen's political lives depended on slavery. The three-fifths formula handed Jefferson his narrow victory in the presidential election of 1800 by inflating the votes of the southern states in the Electoral College.","locateZh":"国父们的政治生命依赖于奴隶制。三分之五公式通过虚增南方各州在选举人团中的票数，让杰斐逊在 1800 年的总统选举中险胜。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文已明示\"奴隶制 → 杰斐逊胜选\"，杰斐逊为国父之一，故\"某些国父在政治上从奴隶制获益\"为真，锁定 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"The three-fifths formula handed Jefferson his narrow victory in the presidential election of 1800 by inflating the votes of the southern states in the Electoral College","opt":"Some Founding Fathers benefit politically from slavery"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Slaves in the old days did not have the right to vote 看似常识为真，但原文从未讨论奴隶投票权——counted a slave as three fifths of a man for purposes of congressional representation 谈的是奴隶在国会代表权计算中被算作五分之三，是\"代表权计算单位\"，不是\"投票权\"，二者不可混。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Slaves owners usually had large savings accounts 把原文比喻 like having a large bank account 当成字面事实理解；原文的本意是\"奴隶就像一笔大额存款\"——奴隶本身相当于资产，并不是说奴隶主真的有大额银行账户。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 Slavery was regarded as a peculiar institution 中 \"was regarded\" 给出一个被动评价；原文 protections for the \"peculiar institution\" 把 \"peculiar institution\" 加引号——这是南方人为奴隶制起的婉称，并非全社会普遍把奴隶制看作\"特殊制度\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"Washington's decision to free slaves originated from his____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moral considerations."},{"key":"B","text":"military experience."},{"key":"C","text":"financial conditions."},{"key":"D","text":"political stand."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"华盛顿释放奴隶的决定源于他的____","choicesZh":{"A":"道德考虑。","B":"军事经历。","C":"财务状况。","D":"政治立场。"},"analysis":{"type":"Q40 问华盛顿释放奴隶决定的起源，答案在原文有直接对应句，属细节题。","parse":"Q40 是不完整陈述句，Washington's decision to free slaves originated from his____，空格在 his 之后，要求填名词短语，结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"Washington, who had begun to believe that all men were created equal after observing the bravery of the black soldiers during the Revolutionary War, overcame the strong opposition of his relatives to grant his slaves their freedom in his will.","locateZh":"华盛顿在独立战争中目睹黑人士兵的英勇之后，已开始相信人人生而平等；他顶住亲属们强烈的反对，最终在遗嘱中赋予自己的奴隶以自由。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 moral considerations 看似与 believe that all men were created equal 相关，但\"相信人人平等\"是华盛顿在\"目睹勇敢\"之后才形成的信念，是中间结果，不是起源；题问 originated from（起源）必须追到最上游的因，即军事经历。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"源于独立战争中的观察\"与 military experience 在语义上完全重合（战争中的观察就是军事经历的一部分），锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"after observing the bravery of the black soldiers during the Revolutionary War","opt":"military experience"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 financial conditions 在原文找不到任何对应：P6 只说华盛顿顶住亲属反对、在遗嘱中释奴，并未涉及任何经济或财务原因；like having a large bank account 谈的是\"奴隶价值\"而非释放奴隶的动机。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 political stand 在文中找不到关于华盛顿\"政治立场推动释奴\"的描述；Washington and Jefferson privately expressed distaste for slavery 只说\"私下反感\"，P5 的政治线讨论的是国父在政治上依赖奴隶制，与\"政治立场推动释奴\"方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"matching","title":"Section II Part B 选句填空","directions":"Directions: In the following text, some segments have been removed. For Questions 41-45, choose the most suitable one from the list A-G to fit into each of the numbered blanks. There are two extra choices, which do not fit in any of the blanks. Mark your answers on ANSWER SHEET 1. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"The time for sharpening pencils, arranging your desk, and doing almost anything else instead of writing has ended. The first draft will appear on the page only if you stop avoiding the inevitable and sit, stand up, or lie down to write. {{41}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"Be flexible. Your outline should smoothly conduct you from one point to the next, but do not permit it to railroad you. If a relevant and important idea occurs to you now, work it into the draft. {{42}} Grammar, punctuation, and spelling can wait until you revise. Concentrate on what you are saying. Good writing most often occurs when you are in hot pursuit of an idea rather than in a nervous search for errors."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"{{43}} Your pages will be easier to keep track of that way, and, if you have to clip a paragraph to place it elsewhere, you will not lose any writing on the other side."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"If you are working on a word processor, you can take advantage of its capacity to make additions and deletions as well as move entire paragraphs by making just a few simple keyboard commands. Some software programs can also check spelling and certain grammatical elements in your writing. {{44}} These printouts are also easier to read than the screen when you work on revisions."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"Once you have a first draft on paper, you can delete material that is unrelated to your thesis and add material necessary to illustrate your points and make your paper convincing. The student who wrote \"The A&P as a State of Mind\" wisely dropped a paragraph that questioned whether Sammy displays chauvinistic attitudes toward women. {{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"Remember that your initial draft is only that. You should go through the paper many times – and then again – working to substantiate and clarify your ideas. You may even end up with several entire versions of the paper. Rewrite. The sentences within each paragraph should be related to a single topic. Transitions should connect one paragraph to the next so that there are no abrupt or confusing shifts. Awkward or wordy phrasing or unclear sentences and paragraphs should be mercilessly poked and prodded into shape."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"段末","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made. 你如何写作并不重要,只要你去写就行。既然你已经将一个主题发展成了一个暂定论点,你就可以整理笔记,开始充实你所制定的大纲。\n第1段末，承“别拖延、坐下就写”，要补一句收束动笔的话 空前 The first draft will appear on the page only if you stop avoiding the inevitable and sit, stand up, or lie down to write 在反复说“别躲了，赶紧用各种姿势写”；空 __(41)__ 落在第1段末尾，下一段第2段另起话题讲“Be flexible”写初稿的注意事项。所以这个空要补一句紧承“你怎么写都行、动笔就对了”的过渡/收束话，把“动笔”这件事接到下文“怎么写”去。\n复现“how you write”接上文，“outline”引下文，两边都缝住 D 句首 It makes no difference how you write, just so you do（你怎么写都无所谓，只要写就行），正好把空前 sit, stand up, or lie down to write 列举的各种写姿一句收住，复现线索对上；句末 begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made 引出“提纲”，把话题往下递，承上启下功能也满足。","options":{},"choiceEn":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made.","clues":["词汇复现 复现“write/how you write” 空前句反复出现“写”这个动作 sit, stand up, or lie down to write，正确句很可能再次用 write/how you write 之类说法呼应“怎么写都行、写就是了”。","结构功能 段末+下段另起，需总收并过渡 下段 Be flexible 另起讲写初稿的具体注意事项，因此这个段末空要补一句能收住“动笔”、并自然引向“接下来该整理笔记/动手展开”的话。"]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"段中","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around. 通过将初稿作为思考你想说什么的手段,你很可能会发现比笔记最初暗示的更多内容。许多优秀作家根本不使用大纲,而是在写作过程中发现组织原则。不要试图在第一遍就写出完美无误的草稿。\n第2段中部，前讲“灵活、想到就写进去”，后讲“语法拼写可等改稿” 空前 If a relevant and important idea occurs to you now, work it into the draft（想到相关重要的点就写进初稿）；空后 Grammar, punctuation, and spelling can wait until you revise（语法标点拼写可以等到修改时再说）。这个段中空要补一句承上“灵活、放手写”、启下“初稿阶段别纠错”的过渡话，核心意思应是“初稿不必求完美”。\n句末“别求一稿完美”正好引出“语法可等改稿”，复现draft G 句末 Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around（别想一次写出完全正确的初稿），与空后 Grammar, punctuation, and spelling can wait until you revise 严丝合缝：正因别求一稿完美，所以语法拼写可以缓到改稿时。G 全句又反复出现 the first draft、a perfectly correct draft，复现 draft 对上，承上启下都站得住。","options":{},"choiceEn":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around.","clues":["逻辑连接 前后句同向递进，共指“初稿别求完美” 空前 work it into the draft 与空后 Grammar, punctuation, and spelling can wait until you revise 方向一致、都在松绑初稿，正确句应顺着这股“初稿阶段放开手、别纠结”的逻辑把话挑明。","词汇复现 复现“draft” 空前出现 into the draft（初稿），正确句很可能再次提到 draft，把“初稿”这个关键词接住。"]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"段首","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper. 为了使修改更容易,留出较宽的页边距和行间距,这样你就可以轻松添加词语、句子和修正。只在纸的一面书写。\n第3段独占段首，下文讲“这样做的好处”，要补一句给出某操作建议的总起句 本空 __(43)__ 居于第3段最前，空后紧跟 Your pages will be easier to keep track of that way, and, if you have to clip a paragraph to place it elsewhere, you will not lose any writing on the other side（这样你的纸页更好管理，要剪贴某段时也不会丢掉背面的字）。下文用 that way、the other side 在解释“某个做法”的好处，所以这个段首空要补一句“提出那个做法”的总起句——而且这做法显然和“纸张的另一面”有关。\n提出“留白+单面书写”的操作，正是that way的先行、the other side的来源 A leave wide margins and extra space between lines 和 Write on only one side of the paper 给出的正是一套具体操作建议，恰好充当空后 that way 的先行词；其中“只写一面”直接对应空后 you will not lose any writing on the other side（背面不丢字）——只有单面写，背面才会有“另一面”的字可保。开头 To make revising easier 也点明这套做法为修改服务，段首总起功能完整。","options":{},"choiceEn":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper.","clues":["代词指代 空后“that way”需先行操作 空后 Your pages will be easier to keep track of that way 里的 that way（那样做）是指示词，必须在所填句里找到它指代的那个“具体做法”作先行词，所以正确句必须先给出一个明确的操作建议。","词汇复现 空后“the other side”指向“纸的单面” 空后 you will not lose any writing on the other side（背面不会丢字）点到“纸的另一面”，正确句里应出现与“纸张/单面书写”有关的复现说法，才能让“the other side”有所指。"]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"段中","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems. 然而,值得记住的是,尽管从打印机打出的干净文稿可能看起来很棒,但它的可读性取决于投入其中的思考和写作。许多作者会审慎地将数据存储在磁盘上,并在每次完成草稿时打印页面,以避免因电源故障或其他问题而丢失任何材料。\n第4段中部，前夸软件查拼写语法，后讲“打印稿”，要补一句衔接“软件→打印”并带提醒的话 空前 Some software programs can also check spelling and certain grammatical elements in your writing（有些软件还能查拼写和部分语法）一直在夸文字处理软件的便利；空后 These printouts are also easier to read than the screen when you work on revisions（这些打印稿比屏幕更便于改稿）。空后用 These printouts（这些打印稿），可上文并没出现“打印稿”——所以这个段中空要补一句既呼应“软件”、又引出“打印”、并给 These printouts 提供先行词的话。\nhowever接住“夸软件”，“print their pages”给These printouts当先行词 C 句首转折 It's worth remembering, however 正好给空前一味夸软件的话泼一盆冷水（再漂亮也看思考），逻辑线索对上；句末 print their pages each time they finish a draft（每写完一稿就打印）引出“打印”，恰为空后 These printouts（这些打印稿）提供了先行词，代词指代线索严丝合缝。","options":{},"choiceEn":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems.","clues":["代词指代 空后“These printouts”需先行“打印” 空后 These printouts are also easier to read than the screen 用 These printouts（这些打印稿）回指，但空前只谈软件、未提打印，所以正确句里必须出现“print/打印”，给 These printouts 提供先行词。","逻辑连接 上文一味夸软件，可能需一句“however”式提醒转一下 空前 Some software programs can also check spelling and certain grammatical elements 都在夸软件好处，正确句若带 however 之类的转折提醒（软件再好，质量仍靠思考），逻辑会更顺，且能自然过渡到“打印”话题。"]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To make revising easier, leave wide margins and extra space between lines so that you can easily add words, sentences, and corrections. Write on only one side of the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"After you have clearly and adequately developed the body of your paper, pay particular attention to the introductory and concluding paragraphs. It's probably best to write the introduction last, after you know precisely what you are introducing. Concluding paragraphs demand equal attention because they leave the reader with a final impression."},{"key":"C","text":"It's worth remembering, however, that though a clean copy fresh off a printer may look terrific, it will read only as well as the thinking and writing that have gone into it. Many writers prudently store their data on disks and print their pages each time they finish a draft to avoid losing any material because of power failures or other problems."},{"key":"D","text":"It makes no difference how you write, just so you do. Now that you have developed a topic into a tentative thesis, you can assemble your notes and begin to flesh out whatever outline you have made."},{"key":"E","text":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces."},{"key":"F","text":"In the final paragraph about the significance of the setting in \"A&P,\" the student brings together the reasons Sammy quit his job by referring to his refusal to accept Lengel's store policies."},{"key":"G","text":"By using the first draft as a means of thinking about what you want to say, you will very likely discover more than your notes originally suggested. Plenty of good writers don't use outlines at all but discover ordering principles as they write. Do not attempt to compose a perfectly correct draft the first time around."}],"answer":"E","explanation":{"answer":"E","type":"段末","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces. 尽管这是一个有趣的问题,但它与论点无关,论点解释的是环境如何影响Sammy辞职的决定。她没有包含那一段,而是增加了一段描述Lengel对女孩们的生硬回应,这样她就可以引出他执行的A & P\"政策\"。\n第5段末，前讲“某学生删掉了一段质疑Sammy的内容”，要补一句承接“那一段”并说明删它原因/改动的话 空前 The student who wrote \"The A&P as a State of Mind\" wisely dropped a paragraph that questioned whether Sammy displays chauvinistic attitudes toward women（那位学生明智地删掉了一段质疑 Sammy 是否有大男子主义的内容）。本空 __(45)__ 在该段末尾，紧承“删掉的那一段”。所以这个空要补一句解释“为什么删它”或“删后改成了什么”的话，话题必须围绕这个被删段、Sammy、论点（thesis）。\nthis issue回指被删段，“nothing to do with the thesis”正解释删因，并交代改动 E 句首 Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis（尽管这是个有趣的问题，但它与论点无关）：this issue 正好回指空前 a paragraph that questioned whether Sammy displays chauvinistic attitudes 提出的那个问题，指代有着落；“与论点无关”直接解释了“为何明智地删它”。E 后半 Instead of including that paragraph, she added one 又交代删后改加了哪段，复现 Sammy、thesis、A&P，呼应严丝合缝。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Although this is an interesting issue, it has nothing to do with the thesis, which explains how the setting influences Sammy's decision to quit his job. Instead of including that paragraph, she added one that described Lengel's crabbed response to the girls so that she could lead up to the A & P \"policy\" he enforces.","clues":["代词指代 正确句须有指示词回指“被删的那一段” 空前刚提到 dropped a paragraph that questioned whether Sammy displays chauvinistic attitudes（删掉的那一段），正确句很可能用 this/that paragraph 回指它，所以正确句里应出现指向“那一段/那个问题”的指示词。","词汇复现 复现“thesis/Sammy/A&P” 空前出现 Sammy 与本文反复出现的 thesis（论点），正确句应再次提到 Sammy、thesis 或 A&P 这类专名，以解释“那一段为何与论点无关”。"]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"In his autobiography, Darwin himself speaks of his intellectual powers with extraordinary modesty. He points out that he always experienced much difficulty in expressing himself clearly and concisely, but (46) he believes that this very difficulty may have had the compensating advantage of forcing him to think long and intently about every sentence, and thus enabling him to detect errors in reasoning and in his own observations. He disclaimed the possession of any great quickness of apprehension or wit, such as distinguished Huxley. (47) He asserted, also, that his power to follow a long and purely abstract train of thought was very limited, for which reason he felt certain that he never could have succeeded with mathematics. His memory, too, he described as extensive, but hazy. So poor in one sense was it that he never could remember for more than a few days a single date or a line of poetry. (48) On the other hand, he did not accept as well founded the charge made by some of his critics that, while he was a good observer, he had no power of reasoning. This, he thought, could not be true, because the \"Origin of Species\" is one long argument from the beginning to the end, and has convinced many able men. No one, he submits, could have written it without possessing some power of reasoning. He was willing to assert that \"I have a fair share of invention, and of common sense or judgment, such as every fairly successful lawyer or doctor must have, but not, I believe, in any higher degree.\" (49) He adds humbly that perhaps he was \"superior to the common run of men in noticing things which easily escape attention, and in observing them carefully.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"Writing in the last year of his life, he expressed the opinion that in two or three respects his mind had changed during the preceding twenty or thirty years. Up to the age of thirty or beyond it poetry of many kinds gave him great pleasure. Formerly, too, pictures had given him considerable, and music very great, delight. In 1881, however, he said: \"Now for many years I cannot endure to read a line of poetry. I have also almost lost my taste for pictures or music.\" (50) Darwin was convinced that the loss of these tastes was not only a loss of happiness, but might possibly be injurious to the intellect, and more probably to the moral character."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"he believes that this very difficulty may have had the compensating advantage of forcing him to think long and intently about every sentence, and thus enabling him to detect errors in reasoning and in his own observations.","refZh":"他认为，正是这种（表达上的）困难，或许反而给他带来了一种弥补性的好处，即迫使他对每一个句子都进行长时间而专注的思考，从而使他能够察觉自己在推理中和观察中所犯的错误。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"he believes that","lit":"他认为","role":"（主句主谓 + that 宾语从句引导词）","note":""},{"en":"this very difficulty may have had the compensating advantage","lit":"这种困难本身可能反而带来了补偿性的好处","role":"（宾语从句主干（主 + 谓 + 宾））","note":"难点： very 作形容词、compensating 取「补偿」义 this very difficulty 中的 very 不是副词「非常」，而是形容词「正是这个、恰恰这个」，译为「正是这种困难/这种困难本身」；compensating advantage 字面是「补偿性的优势」，结合语境是「弥补缺陷反带来的好处」。回填指代：this very difficulty 指上一句的 he always experienced much difficulty in expressing himself clearly and concisely，故可译作「这种（表达上的）困难本身」。"},{"en":"of forcing him to think long and intently about every sentence,","lit":"（即）迫使他对每个句子都进行长时间而专注的思考","role":"（of 引导的介词短语作 advantage 的同位/内容说明）","note":"难点： of + doing 翻成「即……」 advantage of doing 的 of 在汉语里没有对应介词，应转译成「即/那就是」或干脆把 of 后内容直接铺开作 advantage 的内容。intently 译「专注地、聚精会神地」，不要漏译副词。"},{"en":"and thus enabling him to detect errors in reasoning and in his own observations.","lit":"并因此使他得以察觉推理中和自己观察中的错误","role":"（and 并列的现在分词短语，承接前一个 of 短语）","note":"难点： thus 表结果、in reasoning / in his own observations 是并列介词短语 thus = 因此/从而，提示前后是「因→果」关系，必须译出来。enable sb. to do 译「使（某人）能够……」。in reasoning 和 in his own observations 是 errors 后并列的两个介词短语，都修饰 errors，要译成「推理中的错误和自己观察中的错误」，不能合并漏掉其中一项。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"He asserted, also, that his power to follow a long and purely abstract train of thought was very limited, for which reason he felt certain that he never could have succeeded with mathematics.","refZh":"他还断言，自己跟上一长串纯粹抽象思路的能力非常有限，正因为如此，他确信自己在数学上本来也绝不可能取得成功。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"He asserted, also, that","lit":"他还断言/他也声称","role":"（主句主谓 + 插入副词 + that 引导宾语从句）","note":"难点： also 是插入语「也」 also 被逗号隔开作插入语，承接上文「他不承认自己有 Huxley 那种敏捷领悟力」，译为「他还/也」，放在动词前。assert 取「断言、声称、坚称」义，不要弱化为「说」。"},{"en":"his power to follow a long and purely abstract train of thought was very limited,","lit":"他追随一长串纯粹抽象思路的能力非常有限","role":"（宾语从句主干（主语带不定式定语 + 系 + 表））","note":"难点： follow 取「跟上、理解」义；train of thought 是「思路」 follow 在此不是「跟随」，而是「跟上/理解（一条思路）」（熟词僻义 A2）。a train of thought 是固定搭配「一系列思路、一长串思考」，不能字面译成「思想的火车」。a long and purely abstract train of thought = 「一长串纯粹抽象的思路」。very limited 译「非常有限」，不可省「非常」。"},{"en":"for which reason","lit":"因此/由于这个原因","role":"（非限制性定语从句的关系词（= and for that reason））","note":"难点： for which reason = 因此 for which reason 是 and for that reason 的非限定式写法，整体相当于一个连词「因此、出于这个原因」，承接前一分句。中文断开成「正因为如此」「因此」更自然。"},{"en":"he felt certain that he never could have succeeded with mathematics.","lit":"他确信自己从来不可能在数学上获得成功","role":"（定语从句主干（主 + 系 + 表 + that 宾语从句））","note":"难点： could have done 表「与过去事实相反」 never could have succeeded 是虚拟语气的过去式（could have + 过去分词），表示「（过去）本来也不可能成功」。succeed with mathematics 译「在数学上取得成功/搞好数学」。felt certain that = 确信、深信。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"On the other hand, he did not accept as well founded the charge made by some of his critics that, while he was a good observer, he had no power of reasoning.","refZh":"另一方面，对于某些批评者对他提出的「他虽然善于观察，却没有推理能力」的指责，他并不认为是有充分根据的。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"On the other hand,","lit":"另一方面","role":"（句首过渡状语）","note":""},{"en":"he did not accept as well founded the charge made by some of his critics","lit":"他并不认为某些批评者对他提出的指责是有充分根据的","role":"（主句主干（accept...as... 结构，宾语后置）+ 过去分词短语作 charge 的定语）","note":"难点： accept A as B 宾语后置；well founded 译「有根据的」；charge 取「指责」义 本句的真正结构是 accept [the charge…] as [well founded]，因为宾语 the charge made by… that… 太长，被挪到了 as well founded 之后（即 accept as B A 的倒装）。well founded = well-founded，「有充分根据的、站得住脚的」。charge 在此是熟词僻义 A2：不是「费用、电荷」，而是「指责、控告」（made by some of his critics 明确了语境）。整体译「他不认为这些批评者的指责是有根据的」。"},{"en":"that,","lit":"（即）","role":"（that 引导同位语从句，说明 charge 的具体内容）","note":""},{"en":"while he was a good observer,","lit":"尽管他是个善于观察的人/优秀的观察者","role":"（让步状语从句）","note":"难点： while 译「虽然/尽管」 while 在此不是「当……的时候」，而是表让步「虽然、尽管」（A2 熟词僻义），与后半句构成转折。a good observer 译「优秀的观察者/善于观察的人」。"},{"en":"he had no power of reasoning.","lit":"他却没有推理能力","role":"（同位语从句主句）","note":"难点： no power of reasoning 译「没有推理能力」 power of reasoning = 推理能力/推理的能力。结合让步从句，整句指控为「虽然他是好的观察者，但没有推理能力」。这正是达尔文要反驳的对象。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"He adds humbly that perhaps he was \"superior to the common run of men in noticing things which easily escape attention, and in observing them carefully.\"","refZh":"他谦逊地补充说，他或许「在注意到那些容易被人忽略的事物、并加以仔细观察方面，胜过常人」。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"He adds humbly that","lit":"他谦逊地补充说","role":"（主句主谓 + 方式状语 + that 引导宾语从句）","note":"难点： humbly 译「谦逊地」，呼应全文基调 humbly 是副词「谦卑地、谦逊地」，呼应开篇 Darwin himself speaks of his intellectual powers with extraordinary modesty. 的基调。adds 不要译成「加上」，此处是「补充说、又说」。"},{"en":"perhaps he was \"superior to the common run of men","lit":"也许他「胜过/优于普通人」","role":"（宾语从句主干 + 表语（superior to…））","note":"难点： the common run of men 是固定短语「普通人/一般人」 the common run of 是固定搭配，译「普通的、一般的、平庸的」，the common run of men = 普通人、一般人。superior to = 优于、胜过、强过。perhaps 不能漏，体现自谦的不确定语气。注意此处仍在引号内，是达尔文原话。"},{"en":"in noticing things which easily escape attention,","lit":"（在）注意到那些容易被人忽视的事物（方面）","role":"（in + 动名词作 superior to 的范围状语 + which 定语从句修饰 things）","note":"难点： escape attention 译「逃过注意/被忽略」；which 定从前置 escape attention = 逃过注意、不为人察觉、被忽略。things which easily escape attention 字面是「容易逃过注意的事物」，按汉语习惯改前置定语「（那些）容易被人忽略的事物」。in doing 表示「在某方面」，是 superior to sb. in doing 的固定搭配。"},{"en":"and in observing them carefully.\"","lit":"（在）仔细观察它们（方面）","role":"（and 并列第二个 in + 动名词短语 + 副词）","note":"难点： them 回指 things；carefully 译「仔细地」 them 指上一块的 things（容易被忽略的事物），翻译时可不必重复名词，但要让中文读者明确指向。carefully 不要漏，与前句 noticing 的「注意」形成「注意到 → 仔细观察」的递进。整段引号在此结束，照应达尔文自评。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"Darwin was convinced that the loss of these tastes was not only a loss of happiness, but might possibly be injurious to the intellect, and more probably to the moral character.","refZh":"达尔文确信，丧失这些（对诗歌、绘画、音乐的）爱好不仅是一种幸福的丧失，而且可能对智力有害，更有可能对道德品格有害。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Darwin was convinced that","lit":"达尔文确信","role":"（主句主谓 + that 引导宾语从句）","note":"难点： be convinced that 译「确信、深信」 be convinced that = 确信、深信，比 think 语气重得多，必须译出来。"},{"en":"the loss of these tastes was not only a loss of happiness,","lit":"丧失这些爱好不仅是丧失了一种幸福","role":"（宾语从句主干（not only … but …）的前半）","note":"难点： these tastes 回指诗、画、音乐三种爱好；taste 取「爱好/兴趣」义 these tastes 必须回填指代：见上文 poetry of many kinds gave him great pleasure. Formerly, too, pictures had given him considerable, and music very great, delight.，指诗歌、绘画、音乐三种爱好/趣味。taste 在此是「爱好、欣赏力、趣味」（A2 熟词僻义），不是「味道」。the loss of these tastes 译「丧失这些爱好/失去这些趣味」。a loss of happiness = 一种幸福的丧失/失去一种幸福。"},{"en":"but might possibly be injurious to the intellect,","lit":"而且可能对智力有害","role":"（not only … but … 的后半，第一并列）","note":"难点： injurious to 译「对……有害」；might possibly 体现谨慎语气 injurious to = 对……有害的，与下一块 to the moral character 共享 injurious。might possibly 双重不确定，是达尔文一贯的谨慎语气，译「可能、有可能」即可，不要漏。the intellect 译「智力/智识」。"},{"en":"and more probably to the moral character.","lit":"而且更可能对道德品格有害","role":"（and 并列第二个介词短语，共享 injurious）","note":"难点： 省略还原：(injurious) to the moral character；more probably 体现程度递进 本块省略了重复的 be injurious：完整意思是 and (might) more probably (be injurious) to the moral character。more probably 与前文 might possibly 形成程度递进：「可能对智力有害——更可能对道德品格有害」，必须把递进译出。the moral character = 道德品格/道德人格。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: You have just come back from Canada and found a music CD in your luggage that you forgot to return to Bob, your landlord there. Write him a letter to 1)make an apology, and 2)suggest a solution. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: You have just come back from Canada and found a music CD in your luggage that you forgot to return to Bob, your landlord there. Write him a letter to 1)make an apology, and 2)suggest a solution. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear Bob, I am writing to express my sincere apology for forgetting to return the music CD I borrowed from you. After coming back from Canada, I was surprised to find it still lying in my luggage. I truly feel sorry for any inconvenience this may have caused you. To put things right, I would like to suggest a solution. I will post the CD back to you by international express mail this weekend, so that it can reach you as soon as possible. Please let me know your current address. Once again, I apologize for my carelessness and look forward to your reply. Yours sincerely, Li Ming","translation":"亲爱的Bob： 我写这封信是为了就忘记归还向你借的那张音乐CD向你真诚致歉。从加拿大回国后，我惊讶地发现它还躺在我的行李箱里。对于这可能给你带来的任何不便，我深感抱歉。 为了弥补，我想提出一个解决办法。我会在本周末用国际快递把CD寄还给你，好让它尽快到你手中。请把你目前的收件地址告诉我。 再次为我的粗心致歉，并期待你的回复。 此致 Li Ming","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"事由＋致歉一体","text":"【第 1 段】 事由＋致歉一体 。本段用『亮明写信目的』句架开篇（I am writing to express my sincere apology for forgetting to return the music CD），先把致歉意图前置；再用 After coming back from Canada, I was surprised to find it still lying in my luggage 交代情境，让道歉有落点；末句 I truly feel sorry for any inconvenience 补致歉，落实了第一段『称呼＋事由＋致歉』的功能。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"方案落到可执行","text":"【第 2 段】 方案落到可执行 。本段用『引出方案』句架 To put things right, I would like to suggest a solution 起手，再用 I will post the CD back to you by international express mail this weekend, so that ... 把办法写到谁做、怎么做、多久到达，最后 Please let me know your current address 征询对方，方案具体可执行，达成第二段功能。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"呼应致歉＋合规落款","text":"【第 3 段】 呼应致歉＋合规落款 。本段用 Once again, I apologize for my carelessness and look forward to your reply 首尾呼应地收束歉意，再以 Yours sincerely 结尾、署名 Li Ming，既不签真名也不写地址，正好卡住落款的硬约束。"}],"wordCount":108}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1）describe the drawing briefly, 2）explain its intended meaning, and then 3）give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1）describe the drawing briefly, 2）explain its intended meaning, and then 3）give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2008-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画","width":"1188","height":"1160","local":"assets/writing/2008-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, two disabled men, one having lost his left leg and the other his right, tie their remaining legs together, throw away their crutches, and run swiftly in the same direction while supporting each other. Below the picture, a line of words reads: 'You have one leg, I have one leg; together, we can travel everywhere.' Simple as it appears, the drawing conveys a thought-provoking message about the power of cooperation. Neither man could walk far on his own, yet by binding their weaknesses together they turn two disabilities into one working pair of legs. This symbolizes that when people pool their strengths and make up for one another's shortcomings, they can overcome obstacles that no individual could conquer alone. In my view, such a spirit of mutual support deserves our applause, especially in today's competitive society. Whether in a research team where members contribute different expertise, or in a company where colleagues cover each other's blind spots, cooperation multiplies what isolated effort can achieve. Therefore, we should learn to value teamwork, embrace others' strengths, and march forward hand in hand toward shared goals.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的那样，两个残疾人——一个失去了左腿，另一个失去了右腿——把各自剩下的腿绑在一起，扔掉拐杖，互相搀扶着朝同一个方向飞奔。画面下方有一行字写道：“你有一条腿，我有一条腿；我们在一起，就能走遍天下。”\n画面虽简单，却传递出一个关于合作力量的发人深省的信息。两人单靠自己都走不远，但把各自的弱点绑在一起，就把两处残缺变成了一双能走路的腿。这象征着：当人们汇聚彼此的长处、弥补对方的短处，就能战胜任何个人都无法独自跨越的障碍。\n在我看来，这种互助精神值得称赞，在竞争激烈的当今社会尤其如此。无论是科研团队里成员各展所长，还是公司里同事互补盲区，合作都让孤立的努力所能达到的成效成倍放大。因此，我们应学会珍视团队协作，欣赏他人的长处，携手朝着共同目标前进。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"总起加画面文字","text":"【第 1 段】 总起加画面文字 。开头 As is vividly depicted in the cartoon 一句总起，随后按动作顺序客观描述，末句 Below the picture, a line of words reads 补出配图文字，落实了描述段整体到局部的方法，只描述不评论。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"convey与symbolize过桥","text":"【第 2 段】 convey与symbolize过桥 。用 the drawing conveys a message 与 This symbolizes that 两处表意动词，把绑腿画面翻译成合作取长补短的道理，完成由画到义的过渡。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"举例加表态收尾","text":"【第 3 段】 举例加表态收尾 。先 In my view 亮态度，再用 Whether in a research team... or in a company... 举两个现实场景，末句 Therefore, we should 呼吁收尾，让评论落地。"}],"wordCount":190}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 B prepared · 2 D rare · 3 A of · 4 C previously · 5 C Even · 6 A thought · 7 B suggests · 8 D question · 9 B scoring · 10 C mean · 11 B disproportionately · 12 D careers · 13 A affirm · 14 C however · 15 D put down · 16 D valuing · 17 C consequence · 18 A linked · 19 B subjected · 20 A paradoxical \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 A · 22 D · 23 C · 24 B · 25 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 D · 27 C · 28 A · 29 A · 30 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 A · 32 C · 33 B · 34 D · 35 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 D · 37 B · 38 C · 39 A · 40 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"选句填空（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 D · 42 G · 43 A · 44 C · 45 E \n（逐题解析见 选句填空（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
